<title>UK: Brown says cuts gas levy to zero from April 1998.</title>
<headline>Brown says cuts gas levy to zero from April 1998.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said he would be reducing the gas levy imposed by the last Conservative government to zero from April 1998.</p>
<p>Combined with the cut in VAT on fuel bills and other gas price cuts already announced &quot;I expect gas prices to fall in real terms by 5.5 percent this year and 11 percent next year,&quot; Brown told parliament in his budget speech.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
